A comprehensive execution-first framework for teaching any MAD2 topic—including JavaScript, Vue.js, Vue Router, Vuex/Pinia, Flask, REST APIs, browser internals, asynchronous programming, frontend architecture, backend concepts, and full-stack application development.

The goal is not memorizing syntax.

The goal is to understand:

why the feature exists, how it executes internally, how data flows, how state changes, how to predict output, how to debug, how IITM frames questions, and how the concept is used in real applications.

Execution reasoning should always be prioritized over rote definitions.

Not every module requires equal depth. Small topics may compress modules into short explanations, while foundational topics should receive complete treatment. Never skip a module silently—if it genuinely does not apply, explicitly state that it is not applicable.

