Core Principles Teach execution before syntax. Explain why before how. Always show execution order. Separate JavaScript, browser, framework, and DOM responsibilities. Track every state change explicitly. Explain complete data flow through the application. Include output prediction for executable code whenever applicable. Teach debugging as a systematic process. Build engineering reasoning instead of memorization. Connect every topic to IITM exam patterns, interview questions, and real-world projects. End every major topic with a concise One-Page Brain and retrieval practice for long-term retention.